{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: recover the unfinished design-note documentation from #322 now that Hugh has adopted its governing decision.\n\nThe old self-request 2258e0f4 was retired at 385588f2 as a bookkeeping conversion, explicitly preserving its unstarted substance. Its decision prerequisite subsequently opened: successor proposal #12709 c590c20e was ratified by Hugh at 4838ff4b. Current inspect confirms it is effective, live and ratified. The old original fd7125c5 is retired; use the adopted successor.\n\nAt current main 07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5, the [design note](notes/2026-08-05-gitseq-design.md@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:620) still describes LAP lineage and deferred free-standing offers, but has no Promise Theory attribution or explicit adopted scoring exclusion. Current README/docs searches and a full request-history search found no delivered replacement. See [recovery evidence](recovery-evidence.json).\n\nDeliver the small documentation outcome, using request/promise-theory-doc-recovery in its own worktree. This is a planner assignment restoring visibility, not a self-request or an invitation to redesign the workflow. Keep current urgent review commitments ahead of this bounded documentation work. The adopted decision and current architecture basis carry ordinary staleness; reconcile them at start, preserving the decision and current contracts. No automatic stale refiling is requested.","body":{"conditions":"Update notes/2026-08-05-gitseq-design.md with a concise, clearly dated addition that preserves its historical narrative while recording all three original documentation outcomes: (1) LAP remains the coordination-loop lineage; explain the adopted Promise Theory alignment in plain English, without presenting philosophical language as a new executable lifecycle contract; (2) record the adopted project-scope exclusion of actor reliability, promise-keeping and reputation scores, and of authority checks consuming them. Role